## Original Editions (Public Domain): The original 1830 text, as well as any English editions published prior to 1929, are in the public domain. No one owns the exclusive rights to these versions. You, the Church, and anyone else are completely free to copy, host, distribute, and modify these older texts.

## Modern Editions (Copyrighted): The contemporary editions published by The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints include modern chapter headings, footnotes, cross-references, and study guides. These specific additions, alongside some modern translations, are actively copyrighted by Intellectual Reserve, Inc. (the intellectual property entity of the Church). You cannot legally claim ownership of or freely redistribute these modern copyrighted elements.